From 0e4dc8e9883979b04a68f5b84cdfb4e52449977f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:54:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] CP7 P19 staged suite and ladder points (needs
 planning/analysis-stages.sql; not yet runnable)

Native suite CP7_P19_STAGED (12 predeclared cases: 5 native, 3 races, 2 HTTP,
2 browser; docs/cp7/p19/P19_STAGED.json) through the six staged public RPCs:
reassembled staged analysis equals cp7_analysis_native.build on the job's own
stored reference; authority (foreign actor, epoch change, permission loss, no
direct API path, immutable pages); identity (same UUID same job, changed
query, UUIDs owned by the single path, missing/foreign runs, out-of-range
page); source check UNCHANGED -> ARCHIVED_STALE with unchanged pages; the
single path's grid refusal is the same refusal on the staged path with nothing
paged; races (locked job -> worker_active, concurrent steps never run one unit
twice, statement-limit stops recorded as attempts, access change mid-job
fails the job); real Auth/PostgREST flow and revocation; browser: the staged
button, real progress, reload resumes the same request, pages "Target a-b
dari N", Cek sumber, whole readers never called. Probe cp7_p19_staged_probe.py;
P19 Transport workflow matrix entry p19-staged12.

Scale ladder: a STAGED point per history-days value at every size (also in the
rolled-back native case at 100) and a STAGED browser control; declared staged
bounds read back against the installed bounds(); the reassembled analysis is
checked by the frozen contract with its semantic_hash recomputed server side;
witnesses keep header text and every page's bytes/sha256, never one whole
document. P19_SCALE.json: staged caps, control and the recorded staged
exception (owner items 3 and 5; the 3 s target is still measured, never
marked met).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
